  "method": "Sum grams / 100 * declared per-100-g values, then divide by portions. All listed oil, sauces and coating included. Calories and macros are separately declared; differences from 4/9/4 are possible due to rounding/fibre/factors. Most inputs are approximate editorial assumptions, NOT verified labels of user products. Edition 1.2 adds independent child portions. Adult and child totals are calculated separately; no average family portion. Milk volume in ml uses an approximate 1 ml = 1 g conversion for nutrition only. Oil density is assumed 0.92 g/ml. Pork-beef mince is explicitly modelled at 200 kcal/100 g, not a claim about any brand. Edition 1.3: one whole egg is modelled as 55 g edible content (editorial assumption, not a size standard). Quantities with eggs use complete cooking batches; selected portions and leftovers are distinct. Pancake batter is rounded to whole eggs with all batter ingredients scaled together; fillings are scaled only to requested portions. Nutrition for selected pancakes excludes leftover unfilled pancakes, shown separately. Child savoury sauces are included. Version 1.3.1 removes the premade chicken-stock requirement from all recipes; quick sauces are made from water and juices of chicken cooked in the same pan, or from fresh vegetables. The meat juices are already covered by nutritional modelling of chicken, not counted again as a separate ingredient.",
